# Who has to look at what before it merges.
#
# The specification has an owner for a structural reason: it was once forked into
# two copies that each declared themselves normative, disagreed on concrete rules,
# and drifted for months because no single person had to approve a change to the
# contract. That is the failure this file prevents.

# Default — the maintainers.
*                       @alberthflores95

# The ASK specification. Normative, published, and implemented against by other
# people: a change here needs the Spec Author's review.
/definition/            @alberthflores95

# The published manual and the repository's front door.
/platform/docs/         @alberthflores95
/README.md              @alberthflores95
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @alberthflores95

# Licensing, disclosure and the community contract.
/LICENSE                @alberthflores95
/COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md  @alberthflores95
/SECURITY.md            @alberthflores95
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md     @alberthflores95

# The enrichment prompts are rendered from the specification. They are code, but a
# change here changes what the model is told, so they follow the same review path.
/platform/packages/ask-admin-api/src/ask_admin_api/prompts/  @alberthflores95

# CI is what keeps the rest of this honest.
/.github/               @alberthflores95
/scripts/               @alberthflores95
